@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"

Feature: WWW Whitepaper
	Frontend testing for creating a www whitepaper

Setup:
    * I get all test passwords and admin emails

Teardown:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I sign out and sign into www as a user with the email address "${staticWWWAdminEmailAddress}" and password "${staticWWWAdminPassword}"
	* I tear down the following document and media entries
	| Document_1.pdf |

Scenario: Add Whitepaper
	Admins should be able to add a whitepaper on www.

	Given I go to the www homepage
	And I click on the Sign In Create Account footer link
	And I sign into www as a user with the email address "${staticWWWAdminEmailAddress}" and password "${staticWWWAdminPassword}"
	And I navigate to the Product Menu and go to the "Documents and Media" portlet under the "Content & Data" category under the "Site Administration" panel
	And I close the product menu
	And I go to the documents and media folder "RESOURCES"
	And I go to the documents and media folder "whitepapers"
	And I go to a new form for a marketing asset document
	And I expand the "Custom Fields" header in the document bottom panel
	And I expand the "Categorization" header in the document bottom panel
	And I populate the following documents and media fields and values
	| File                 |                    | Document_1.pdf                                                            |
	| Primary Buyer Stage  | Select             | Evaluation                                                                |
	| Cover Image          | File Upload        | RESOURCES,whitepapers,Business Whitepaper Covers,Digital by Default Cover |
	| Seo Description      | Bottom Panel Input | Test Seo Description                                                      |
	| Seo Title            | Bottom Panel Input | Test Seo Title                                                            |
	| Category List Filter | Category Select    | Resources                                                                 |
	| Language             | Category Select    | English                                                                   |
	| Resource Type        | Category Select    | Whitepapers                                                               |
	| Topic                | Category Select    | Customer Experience                                                       |
	And I click the document publish button
	And I sign out of www
	And I go to the www page with the url "resources"
	And I filter the resources in the Resource Library using the following filters and values
	| Resource Types | Whitepapers |
	Then I should be able to view the resource with the title "Document_1.pdf"